<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38860" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōpălo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a.
			propalam, <i>to make public</i> or <i>manifest</i>, <i>to divulge</i>
			(post-class.), <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propalata et publica veritas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Oros. 6, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">divinitus propalatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 137</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nondum propalatam esse sanctorum viam,</span>”
				<i>thrown open</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Heb. 9, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
